This page follows up on [incidents/4471](/kb/incidents/4471). That page was closed with
"Closed. One issue, one fix, no follow-ups." This page re-reads the same 412 merged reports
with the kb's own fingerprint rule and finds that the merge was coarser than the data.

## What the merge did, and what the data says

The night's triage ran on [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject): merge by
subject line. That rule is fast and needs no reading - but `fingerprint.ts` says a report's
issue is decided by **where it came from** (the reporter's tenant, `places.ts`) and **which
server code it raises**, not by what intake guessed or how the subject reads.

Run over the export, the same 412 reports split like this:

<ClusterTable ticket={4471} />

Three rows: one issue with a ticket of its own, and two clusters merged into #4471 that no
ticket of their own covers. Same code from a different place is a different bug:
`tram-3:E-TZ-114` is not `sched-prod:E-TZ-114`, and `rota-6:E-SYNC-04` shares nothing with
either except the night.

## The three issues, as filed

One ticket per issue, filed in the public repo
[RafalWojciechRolsky/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows-r2](https://github.com/RafalWojciechRolsky/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows-r2):

1. [sched-prod · E-TZ-114 · shifts moved by an hour](https://github.com/RafalWojciechRolsky/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows-r2/issues/1) -
   349 reports, 206 people, 03:12 → 06:13. This is what #4471 properly is.
2. [tram-3 · E-TZ-114 · platform screens one hour behind the timetable](https://github.com/RafalWojciechRolsky/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows-r2/issues/2) -
   44 reports, 26 people, 03:33 → 06:11. Reporter domains: tramvaj-ostrava.cz, metro-lund.se,
   ml-trafik.se - all tram-3 tenants, whatever intake tagged them.
3. [rota-6 · E-SYNC-04 · night rota listed twice](https://github.com/RafalWojciechRolsky/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows-r2/issues/3) -
   19 reports, 9 people, 03:27 → 06:08. Reporter domains: oak-lane-care.co.uk,
   lindholm-hus.se. Night shifts shown twice, an hour apart, in care homes - the
   safety-relevant one.

Every count on this page is computed at render time from `src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`
by the kb's own components; the tickets carry the same numbers from the same file.

## The night

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Outcome

The desk kept working while this page was written. The engineering update on the challenge
page (18 October 2026) records the outcomes:

- **rota-6** - fixed, change #31 (the sync fix landed). The repo's ticket is closed as
  completed.
- **tram-3** - won't fix, the boards are retired. The repo's ticket is closed as not
  planned.
- **sched-prod** - stays what it always was: #4471 itself, closed with its fix, change #29,
  shipped at 06:15.

<Callout>
Desk update, 18 October 2026: rota-6 fixed by change #31 (sync fixed); tram-3 won't fix -
boards retired. The two extra tickets are closed in the repo per those outcomes.
</Callout>

## Why this page exists

- A big night is mostly one bug reported many times - but not always. The subject rule
  sweeps; the fingerprint rule checks. Reading both costs minutes.
- The page's numbers are computed, not typed; the desk ref below is derived, not decorated.

